# What prim does not format, in gitignore syntax.
#
# Since prim 0.3.0 these entries hold however prim is invoked. Up to 0.2.4 they
# applied to a directory walk only, and `prim fmt <path>` rewrote an ignored
# file named explicitly (driftsys/prim#98); every gate here still points at a
# directory, so nothing depended on the change. `--no-primignore` is the
# deliberate override.
#
# prim honours .gitignore on top of this file, but only where .gitignore
# actually covers the path — checked entry by entry below rather than assumed.

# dprint.json's excludes, carried forward so the migration did not widen which
# files a formatter may rewrite. Four of its six are here; `**/target` is the
# fifth and `/target` in .gitignore covers it. The sixth was
# `.claude/worktrees/**`, and `.claude/` below covers more than that.
corpus/
goldens/

# Unity writes the UPM package's `.meta` files and a formatter must not rewrite
# them: the guid inside one is what an asset reference resolves through, and in
# an immutable Git-URL package nothing can mint a replacement.
#
# **All but one are already safe**, which is why this is a rule rather than a
# tidy-up. prim skips a `.meta` as "not a file type prim formats" — except
# `LICENSE.meta`, whose name before the final dot is
# `LICENSE`, a name prim does format. Measured: `prim fmt` strips the trailing
# space Unity writes after `userData:`, `assetBundleName:` and
# `assetBundleVariant:` in that one file, and leaves the eleven identically
# shaped ones alone. Same root as the `LICENSE`-not-`LICENSE.md` note in
# unity/com.driftsys.dashscene/README.md.
unity/com.driftsys.dashscene/**/*.meta
**/node_modules
**/.git-std

# Agent tooling, none of it tracked. .gitignore covers only `.claude/worktrees/`,
# so `.claude/skills/` and its siblings were inside prim's walk — measured, a
# file there is reported by `prim fmt --check .`. Without this entry the
# pre-commit hook rewrites a developer's own untracked content and `just lint`
# fails on files CI never sees.
.claude/

# `git std bump` writes this file, and prim would hard-wrap it. The two would
# fight once per release: the pre-commit hook rewraps what the bump generated,
# and the bump after that regenerates it unwrapped, so `just prim` goes red on a
# diff nobody wrote. prim's own recipes.md prescribes this entry for a repository
# using git-std and says prim ships it as a default — measured on 0.2.4 and again
# on 0.3.0, it does not. No CHANGELOG.md exists here yet; the first
# `just release` creates one.
/CHANGELOG.md

# The workspace Cargo.toml was here too, until prim 0.3.0. Its TOML formatter
# collapsed an array nested in an inline table onto one line and ignored
# max_line_length while doing it, which took that file to 198 columns from 91
# (driftsys/prim#96). Fixed, and measured on the real manifest: 0.3.0 leaves it
# at 91 columns and 335 lines, changing only the indent of two feature lists from
# four spaces to the two `.editorconfig` already asked for. So it is in scope,
# and no manifest in the tree is excluded.
docs/archive/
